The transition library in prism_terminal/core/reel_web.py (the `.cut-push`,
`.cut-push-up`, `.cut-squeeze` and `.cut-zoom` rules inside _HARNESS_CSS) is
adapted from HyperFrames' CSS transition catalogue — specifically the "Push
Slide", "Vertical Push", "Squeeze" and "Zoom Through" entries.

Adapted rather than copied: the originals are GSAP timelines, and Prism's
renderer films a paused page by setting each frame's time by hand, so they
were rewritten as pure functions of Prism's own `--x` and `--e` progress
variables. The motion each one describes is theirs; the implementation is not
shared with the original.

